            <ArticleTitle>Warm heart surgery in patients with cold autoimmune disorders.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>532-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Continuous warm antegrade delivery of cardioplegia while maintaining systemic normothermia is a new method of performing coronary artery bypass grafting. It can be used to avoid the detrimental effects of hypothermia in patients with cold autoimmune disease.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
